## Summary

The bug was in `codex-rs/tui/src/chatwidget.rs` in the message submission logic (`submit_user_message_with_history_and_shell_escape_policy`). The code explicitly dropped the permission profile to `None` whenever the session's sandbox policy was the legacy `SandboxPolicy::ExternalSandbox` variant:

```rust
let permission_profile = if matches!(
    self.config.permissions.sandbox_policy.get(),
    SandboxPolicy::ExternalSandbox { .. }
) {
    None
} else {
    Some(self.config.permissions.permission_profile())
};
```

Now it always preserves the profile from session configuration, regardless of the active sandbox policy variant:

```rust
let permission_profile = Some(self.config.permissions.permission_profile());
```

The submitted `Op::UserTurn` now carries the configured permission profile even under the external sandbox variant. The `SandboxPolicy` import remains used elsewhere in the file, and `cargo check -p codex-tui` passes.
